meta {
  name: Create Page/Form Org Mapping
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/page-org-map?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "org_id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
    "page_id": "123456789",
    "form_id": "2217695302333588",
    "platform": "fb"
  }
}

docs {
  Registers which branch (org) a Meta Page — and optionally one specific lead
  form — belongs to. Requires super_admin. The row is written under the tenant
  named by ?tenant_id=, never the caller's own.

  Required before any lead from that form can be synced: the webhook resolves
  org_id from (tenant_id, form_id) here, falling back to the page-level row.

  form_id is OPTIONAL and nullable. Omit it to create the PAGE-LEVEL catch-all
  that routes every form on the page, which is the main thing the admin screen
  creates and which this API previously made impossible (the schema demanded
  form_id even though the column is nullable). An exact form_id row always wins
  over the page-level row for that page.

  Regression checks:
    * omit form_id entirely        -> 201, and the row has form_id NULL
    * repeat the same page+form    -> 409 naming the org that holds it
                                      (constraint uq_meta_page_form_org_map)
    * second page-level row, same page and both active
                                   -> 409 saying a page may have at most one
                                      active page-level row
                                      (uq_meta_page_form_org_map_page_level)
    * org_id belonging to ANOTHER tenant
                                   -> 400; the RLS WITH CHECK refuses it, so the
                                      row is never written. THIS is the
                                      cross-tenant leak test — a super admin
                                      must not be able to point tenant A's page
                                      at tenant B's branch.
    * caller below super_admin     -> 403
}
